  "_note_float32_boundary": "T is float32; float32(1/365)=0.0027397261001 > 1/365=0.0027397260274, so `T > 1/365` keeps the 1-day contracts and `T <= 1/365` selects exactly T==0. The basis='days' strata are bucketed on days=round(T*365) instead; the basis='T' strata use the exact comparisons and are always emitted.",
  "_note_dataset": "v4 applies T > 1 day at export, so the T==0 and 0<T<=1day strata are EMPTY by construction and the decoder-degeneracy ceiling does not bind. That is the intended outcome of the v4 preprocessing, not a failed diagnostic.",
  "_note_liquidity_strata": "basis='liquidity' rows (bid_pos: best_bid > 0; relspread_le1: (ask-bid)/mid <= 1, which is bounded by 2 when bid >= 0; and their intersection) are REPORTING strata only. NOTHING is dropped for liquidity anywhere in this pipeline -- every other row in this file still covers the whole sample. Empty on v3, which has no best_bid/best_offer datasets."
